# .claudeignore — paths Claude must never read into context.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT READ BY CLAUDE CODE ON ITS OWN. Measured 2026-08-19 against the
# 2.1.235 binary: the string "claudeignore" appears 0 times, ".gitignore" appears 95.
# The mechanism that actually gates a read is a `Read(<glob>)` entry in the
# `permissions.deny` list of a settings file ("deny reading within the sandbox.
# Merged with paths from Read(", same binary).
#
# So this file is the SOURCE, and `scripts/claudeignore_sync.py` compiles it into
# `~/.claude/settings.json`. Edit here, then run:
#
#     python3 scripts/claudeignore_sync.py            # report only
#     python3 scripts/claudeignore_sync.py --fix      # write the deny rules
#
# settings.json is read ONCE at process start, so a change applies at the next launch,
# never to the running session.
#
# Rule of thumb: generated, vendored, minified or huge. Never a receipt. store/ stays
# readable on purpose — persisted receipts there are evidence (memory
# `the-answer-was-already-on-disk-as-a-receipt`), and only its caches are blocked.

# Vendored dependencies
**/node_modules/**

# Build output
**/.next/**
**/dist/**
**/build/**
**/bin/Debug/**
**/bin/Release/**
**/obj/**
**/.turbo/**
**/storybook-static/**
**/playwright-report/**
**/test-results/**

# Lockfiles: thousands of lines, and never the answer to a question
**/package-lock.json
**/pnpm-lock.yaml
**/yarn.lock
**/uv.lock
**/packages.lock.json

# Minified and mapped assets
**/*.min.js
**/*.min.css
**/*.map

# Coverage and profiling
**/coverage/**
**/htmlcov/**
**/.pytest_cache/**
**/.ruff_cache/**
**/__pycache__/**

# Logs
**/*.log

# Generated knowledge graph — 8.1 MB, rebuilt by a post-commit hook
graphify-out/**

# Virtualenvs
.venv/**
**/.venv/**

# Regenerated engine caches. NOT store/ as a whole: dossiers and *.lint.json are receipts.
store/_cache/**
store/golden_runs/**
store/control_center/runs/**

# Binary content
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.gif
**/*.pdf
**/*.zip
**/*.bundle
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
